{"name":"Notorious","hex":"#bda998","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"notorious","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Senses with an unfavourable connotation.\nOf a person or entity: generally or widely known for something negative; infamous.","Of a person or entity: generally or widely known for something negative; infamous."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Synonym of notoriously."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/notorious"}],"entries":[{"title":"Notorious (1946 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Notorious is a 1946 American spy film noir directed and produced by Alfred Hitchcock, starring Cary Grant, Ingrid Bergman, and Claude Rains as three people whose lives become intimately entangled during an espionage operation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Notorious_%281946_film_poster%29.jpg/330px-Notorious_%281946_film_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notorious_(1946_film)","wikidata":"Q587419"},{"title":"Notorious (Duran Duran album)","blocks":[{"text":"Notorious is the fourth studio album by the English pop rock band Duran Duran, released on 24 November 1986 by EMI Records. Produced by the band with Nile Rodgers, its musical style differed from the band's previous albums with a funk rock sound. It is the first album to feature the band as a trio with singer Simon Le Bon, keyboardist Nick Rhodes and bassist John Taylor, as drummer Roger Taylor and guitarist Andy Taylor both left by the time the album was released. Andy Taylor would later be replaced by former Missing Persons guitarist Warren Cuccurullo, who completed recording parts of the album in addition to Rodgers and session drummer Steve Ferrone."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2c/Duran_Duran_-_Notorious.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik